\bigcirc - \Delta &= -5\end{align*} Substituting this into the first equation, we get \begin{align*}3\Delta + 4(\Delta - 5) &= 21\\ 7\Delta - 20 &= 21\\ 7\Delta &= 41\\ \Delta &= \frac{41}{7}\end{align*} Substituting this back into the equation \begin{align*}\bigcirc - \Delta &= -5\end{align*}, we get \begin{align*}\bigcirc - \frac{41}{7} &= -5\\ \bigcirc &= \frac{41}{7} + 5\\ \bigcirc &= \frac{41 + 35}{7}\\ \bigcirc &= \frac{76}{7}\end{align*} The sum of two circles is \begin{align*}2\bigcirc &= 2\left(\frac{76}{7}\right)\\ &= \frac{152}{7}\end{align*} So the answer is \begin{align*}\boxed{\frac{152}{7}}\end{align*} <answer> \frac{152}{7} </answer>

